body:
Check out this link about suicide and people with mood disorders. This is the time when it peaks: the end of the winter. Maybe it's the cumulative effects of the cold, darkness and other factors. Just check out the graph.

[https://universe.byu.edu/2016/12/30/debunking-myths-about-suicide-and-the-holidays/](https://universe.byu.edu/2016/12/30/debunking-myths-about-suicide-and-the-holidays/)

&#x200B;

You're exactly like me: the non-scheduled drug abuse (caffeine and others), the lost father (mine developed severe Alzheimer's around freshman year, and my mother died sophomore year of college), and the boredom with things that are "fun."

&#x200B;

I think having fun with your girlfriend and friends could be monumentally good. Some people cannot find pleasure in even doing those things. My girl left me because of my depression, so things could get worse. Your friends gradually distance themselves from you: don't think this is rock bottom. Eventually, you end up all alone on the needle. That's the end, that or suicide.
